-- One scan of BigQuery that both counts and samples the transactions sent to the 1k most-called contracts
-- (examples/most_called_0_8/gas_data/inputs_most_called.txt), for scripts/gas_mainnet_replay.py.
-- The list of targets is generated by `gas_mainnet_replay.py make-bigquery-query <addresses>` (between the markers).
--
-- Same period and definition as the ranking that selected the contracts (examples/most_called_0_8/
-- contract_list_all.csv: direct transactions since 2021-01-01, computed between 2026-01-30 and 2026-03-04), so every
-- contract is evaluated on the same period and every one has calls in it:
--   - period: blocks 11,565,019 (2021-01-01 00:00:00 UTC) to 24,580,372 (2026-03-03 23:59:59 UTC);
--   - direct transactions (to_address = the contract), as in the ranking; internal calls are not sampled;
--   - successful transactions only (receipt_status = 1): failed ones are often trivial reverts.
-- The transactions span several forks: every sampled transaction is replayed under the current rules (Prague), the
-- same for the original, solc and grey; its own fork is used only to check that the original replay reproduces the
-- receipt (prestate check).
--
-- Buckets: per contract, each selector of its ABI (keccak of the canonical signatures, computed from
-- examples/most_called_0_8/etherscan/<address>.json), plus one 'other' bucket with every call whose selector is not
-- in the ABI (junk selectors sent to MEV contracts, fallback/receive, calls without calldata). The contracts whose ABI
-- has no functions (proxies, bots dispatching in the fallback) are bucketed by the raw 4-byte selector instead
-- ('nodata' for calls without one): for proxies these are the functions of the implementation.
-- Sample: per bucket, the 25 transactions with the smallest FARM_FINGERPRINT(hash): a deterministic, reproducible
-- random sample over the whole period (25 to keep spares; 20 are used; the LIMIT of ARRAY_AGG must be a literal).
-- Counts: approximate number of transactions per bucket, to weight the results by frequency.
--
-- Cost (on-demand billing is by bytes read): only the transactions table is read, and only the columns below
-- (hash, block_number, block_timestamp, to_address, input, receipt_status). input dominates the bytes and cannot be
-- avoided (it holds the selector). The block_timestamp filter prunes the daily partitions. ARRAY_AGG ... ORDER BY ...
-- LIMIT is a top-k per group, so the busiest buckets (millions of calls) do not need a full sort.
-- Before running it (on a single line):
--   bq query --dry_run --use_legacy_sql=false < scripts/gas/bigquery/sample_txs.sql
-- Run, writing the result to a table, then read it (small: one row per contract and bucket):
--   bq query --use_legacy_sql=false --destination_table=<project>:grey_gas.sample_txs --replace < scripts/gas/bigquery/sample_txs.sql
--   bq --format=json head -n 100000 <project>:grey_gas.sample_txs > sample_txs.json
